$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3,5-Diphenyl-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (7a).
Typical Stille procedure (Table 2). To a stirred mixture of
3,5-dichloro-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (1) (50 mg, 0.273 mmol) and
(Ph3P)2PdCl2 (9.6 mg, 0.0137 mmol) in MeCN (2 mL) at ca. 20 °C protected
with a CaCl2 drying tube, tributylphenyltin (220 mg, 0.60 mmol) was
added. The mixture was then heated to ca. 100 °C until no starting
material remained (by TLC). The reaction mixture was then cooled to ca.
20 °C and adsorbed onto silica. Dry flash chromatography (hexane/DCM,
7:3) gave the title compound 7a (68 mg, 95%) as yellow needles, identical
to that described above. 3,5-Di(thien-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one
(7m), yield 92%. mp 175-177 °C (from cyclohexane); Rf 0.42 (hexane/DCM,
7:3); (found: C, 47.5; H, 2.1; N, 10.1. C11H6N2OS3 requires C, 47.5; H,
2.2; N, 10.1%); λmax(DCM)/nm 430 (log ε 4.31), 406 (4.40), 388 inf
(4.30), 369 inf (4.11), 261 (4.03), 327 (3.74); νmax/cm-1 3103w, 1614s,
1574w, 1504m, 1450m, 1410s, 1385s, 1350w, 1263m, 1223m, 1080m, 1045m,
997m, 914w, 874m, 853s, 814m, 787w, 739s, 731s, 716s; δH(500 MHz; CDCl3)
8.28 (2H, d, J 4.0, thienyl H-3), 7.64 (2H, d, J 5.0, thienyl H-5), 7.19
(2H, dd, J 4.5, 4.0, thienyl H-4); δC(125 MHz; CDCl3) 161.3 (s), 154.1
(s), 136.4 (s), 133.2 (d), 132.1 (d), 127.7 (d); m/z (EI) 278 (M+, 49%),
141 (100), 114 (6), 109 (36), 97 (8), 83 (6), 71 (11), 64 (7), 58 (14).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium Catalyzed C-C Coupling Reactions of
3,5-Dichloro-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one
