$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (10) Typical Procedure: a mixture of 1 (442
mg, 1 mmol), 1-iodonaphthalene (2b, 279 mg, 1.1 mmol), Pd2dba3 (23 mg,
0.05 equiv of Pd) and AsPh3 (31 mg, 0.10 mmol) in DMF (4 mL) was purged
with N2 for 10 min at room temperature and stirred under N2 at 60 °C for
2.5 h. The reaction mixture was then diluted with water and extracted
with ether. The organic phase was washed twice with water, dried (Na2SO4)
and evaporated. Chromatography of the residue (525 mg) on silica gel (21
g) using CH2Cl2/AcOEt = 99/1 as eluent gave 3b. 3f: oil. [α]D +48°; IR
3437, 1741, 1720, 1710, 1499, 1367, 1168 cm-1; 1H NMR δ 1.43 (9H, s,
t-Bu), 3.10 (1H, dd, J = 13.5, 6.1 Hz, CHH), 3.19 (1H, dd, J = 13.5, 5.5
Hz, CHH), 3.74 (3H, s, CO2Me), 3.95 (3H, s, ArCO2Me), 4.63 (1H, m, α-CH),
5.06 (1H, d, J = 8.3 Hz, NH), 7.21-8.26 (8H, m, ArH).
