$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method D: A mixture of
1-phenyl-4-(tributylstannyl)-1H-1,2,3-triazole (100 mg, 0.23 mmol.),
halogenated derivative (12) (0.27 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (3 mg, 0.004 mmol)
and LiCl (29.3 mg, 0.69 mmol) was irradiated at the temperature and
during the appropriate time under Argon in a focused microwave reactor
DiscoverTM (CEM). The crude products 13a-g were purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel using a mixture of hexane:ethyl acetate as
the eluent. 2-(1-phenyl-1H-1,2,3-triazol-4-yl)pyrazine 13e. Method D.
2-iodopyrazine 12e (56.8 mg, 0.27 mmol) were used. The crude was purified
with a mixture of hexane:ethyl acetate (8:1) as the eluent, 13e (47 mg,
91%) was obtained as a colorless oil. 1H-NMR (CDCl3) δ 9.5 (s, 1H, H-Py),
8.6 (s, 1H, H-5), 8.6-8.5 (m- 2H, H-Py), 7.8 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H, o-H Ph),
7.5 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H, m-H Ph), 7.4 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H, p- H Ph).
13C-NMR (CDCl3) δ 146.6, 145.7, 144.1, 143.9, 142.3, 136.7, 129.9, 129.2,
120.9, 120.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Stille reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
