$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for the Stille coupling of
aryl bromide with vinylstannane 3 (Table 1, entry 1).
4-Vinylacetophenone: To 4-bromoacetophenone (199 mg, 1.00 mmol, 1.00
equiv), vinylstannane (795 mg, 1.20 mmol, 1.20 equiv) and 1,4-dioxane (3
mL, 0.3 M) under argon was added Pd((t-Bu)3)2 (13 mg, 0.0250 mmol, 2.50
mol%). After 16 h of stirring at room temperature, the solution was
concentrated under reduced pressure. CH2Cl2 (2 mL) was added to dissolve
the residue and the phosphonium salt was precipitated by hexanes (20 mL)
addition. The heterogeneous solution was decanted and the solid was
redissolved in CH2Cl2 (2 mL) and reprecipitated upon hexanes (20 mL)
addition. The hexanes layers were concentrated under reduced pressure to
afford the tin-free coupling product. Flash chromatography (0 to 10%
hexanes in CH2Cl2) gave the product as a colorless oil.
2-Vinylanthracene, yield 185 mg, 91%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Removal, Recovery, and Recycling of Triarylphosphonium-Supported Tin
Reagents for Various Organic Transformations
