$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Stille reaction. General procedure A. A
mixture of the pyrazinone 1a-c (0.25 mmol), tetraalkyl- or tetraphenyltin
(0.3mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.015 mmol) in DMF (3 ml) was irradiated at 150
°C for 5 min at 150 W maximum power. The reaction mixture was cooled to
room temperature, extracted with diethyl ether (3×10 ml) and washed with
brine. The combined organic layers were dried over magnesium sulfate and
the crude product was purified by column chromatography over silica gel
(DCMEA 95:5 or DCM-hexane 95:5) to give alkylated- or arylated compound
2a-g. 2c, yield 91%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, yield depends on reaction conditions, Stille
coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave-enhanced transition metal-catalyzed decoration of
2(1H)-pyrazinone scaffolds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
