$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure (GP 3) for
Palladium-Catalyzed Stille Coupling of (S,S)-7 and rac-8. Under argon,
(S,S)-7 (96 mg, 0.2 mmol) or rac-8 (100 mg, 0.3 mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (1 mol
%), and rac-BINAP (2.2 mol %) were dissolved in toluene (2 mL). After
addition of the stannane (1.2 equiv), the mixture was heated to reflux
until the starting material was completely consumed (TLC analysis). The
solution was concentrated in vacuo, and the resulting product was
isolated by column chromatography (SiO2). Synthesis of (S,S)-12e.
Following GP 3 using (S,S)-7 and allytributyltin gave 83.5 mg (91%) of
(S,S)-12e as a white solid and as a single isomer. Mp. 135 °C; [α]D
-38.40 (c 1.88, MeOH ); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.76 (d, 2H, J = 7.9
Hz), 7.40-7.39 (m, 2H), 7.29-7.20 (m, 5H), 6.01-5.87 (m, 1H), 5.19-5.10
(m, 3H), 4.60-4.57 (m, 1H), 3.48 (d, 2H, J = 6.7 Hz), 3.33 (s, 3H),
3.24-3.07 (m, 2H), 1.41 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 179.9, 155.3,
146.9, 137.1, 135.8, 135.4, 129.7, 129.6, 128.1, 127.2, 126.4, 117.3,
79.2, 57.4, 44.1, 40.0, 38.7, 28.4; IR (neat, cm-1) 3382, 2927, 1681,
1527; MS (EI, m/z) 442 (M+); HRMS of [M]+: Calcd. 442.1926; found
442.1926. The product proved to be very unstable, and rapid decomposition
occurred.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and palladium-catalyzed coupling reactions of enantiopure
p-bromophenyl methyl sulfoximine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cho, Gae Young; Okamura, Hiroaki; Bolm, Carsten
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2005), 70(6), 2346-2349

