$DATUM 4,7-Bis[4-(2-ethyhexyl)-2-thienyl]-2,1,3-benzothiadiazole (S9). S8 (7.2
mmol), 4,7-Dibromobenzo[c]-1,2,5-thiadiazole (881.9 mg, 3.0 mmol) and
(Ph3P)2PdCl2 (63.2 mg, 0.09 mmol) were dissolved in anhydrous THF (60 mL)
under argon and refluxed overnight. The solvent was evaporated in vacuum
and a crude product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel
in hexane/dichloromethane (50:3 by vol.). The crude product was
recrystallized by ethanol to give product Orange solid (1.77 g, 91%). 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δH (ppm) = 0.89-0.97 (m, 12H), 1.28-1.44 (m, 16H),
1.63-1.71 (m, 2H), 2.65 (d, J = 6.85 Hz, 4H), 7.01-7.04 (m, 2H), 7.83 (s,
2H), 7.96 (d, J = 1.22 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δC (ppm) =
152.65, 143.03, 138.81, 129.47, 126.03, 125.46, 122.42, 40.34, 34.71,
32.54, 28.92, 25.69, 23.07, 14.14, 10.87. ESI-MS: Mcalcd. = 524.24,
Mfound = 524.2.
