$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General coupling procedure The mixture of bromosubstituted heteroarene
(0.5 mmol), PdCl3(PPh3)2 (0.025 mmol) and ferrocenylstannane 2 or 5 (0.55
mmol) in dry DMF (4 ml) was stirred at 120-130 °C for the time given in
the Table. After the mixture was cooled to room temperature, water (8 ml)
was added and the resulting solution was extracted with ether or
dichloromethane. The organic layer was sequentially washed with saturated
KF solution and water, dried over MgSO4, and evaporated the solvent to
gave a residue which was purified by chromatography on silica gel column
(eluant: petroleum/acetone in the ratio, which was determined by the TLC
studies of each product). 3a, yield 91%. 1H NMR(CDCl3), 2.26(S, 6H),
3.20(d, 1H, J=12.8), 3.92(d, 1H, J=12.8), 4.12(s, 5H), 4.38(m, 2H),
4.69(m, 1 H), 7.30(d, 1H, J=3.88), 7.49(d, 1H, J=3.88), 7.95-7.50(m, 5H);
IR(KBr) 3088, 1626, 1471, 1106, 1019; MS(EI), 429(M+, 100), 385(M-44,
67.16), 105(25.66), 77(14.62), 58(14.49).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
