$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Stille Coupling:
Preparation of Trifluoromethanesulfonic Acid
2-[Benzyl-(4-methoxy-2-phenylbut-2-enoyl)-amino]phenyl Ester (10). A
stirred mixture of Pd2dba3·CHCl3 (6 mg, 0.006 mmol), P(2-furyl)3 (12 mg,
0.051 mmol), and freshly distilled N-methylpyyrolidinone (NMP, 2 mL) was
deoxygenated by bubbling Ar through a submerged needle for 1 h, during
which time a bright yellow solution resulted. A deoxygenated solution of
stannane 9 (200 mg, 0.28 mmol), iodobenzene (52 mg, 0.25 mmol), and NMP
(5 mL) was then added via syringe. Copper(I) iodide (46 mg, 0.28 mmol)
was then added, and the resulting mixture was flushed with a stream of Ar
for 15 min and then maintained at room temperature for 24 h. After
diluting the reaction with EtOAc (100 mL), the resulting solution was
washed with 5% aqueous NH4OH (3 × 10 mL) and brine (3 × 10 mL). The
organic layer was dried (Na2SO4) and filtered, and the filtrate was
concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography (1:9-3:7
EtOAc-hexanes). Trifluoromethanesulfonic acid
2-{benzyl-[4-methoxy-2-(3-methyl-2-nitrophenyl)but-2-enoyl]amino}phenyl
ester (11f). The general procedure for the Stille coupling was followed
using stannane 9 (1.99 g, 2.76 mmol), 1-iodo-3-methyl-2-nitrobenzene (874
mg, 3.31 mmol), Pd2dba3·CHCl3 (214 mg, 0.21 mmol, 7.5 mol%), P(2-furyl)3
(386 mg, 3.66 mmol, 0.6 equiv), and CuI (580 mg, 3.04 mmol, 1.1 equiv) in
NMP (17 mL). The crude residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexanes-ethyl acetate, 11:1-4:1, v/v) to give 11f (1.4 g,
2.5 mmol, 90%, 85:15 mixture of amide rotamers) as a viscous pale yellow
oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, major rotamer) δ 6.84-7.58 (m, 10H), 6.65
(d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 6.37 (dd, J = 8.0, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.93 (t, J = 5.8 Hz,
1H), 5.68 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 4.30 (dd, J = 14.4, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 4.23
(dd, J = 14.4, 6.1 Hz, 1H), 4.05 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 3.34 (s, 3H), 2.16
(s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.4, 148.8, 145.9, 139.2, 136.2,
134.8, 133.7, 132.9, 132.1, 131.4, 130.6, 130.0, 129.4, 128.9, 128.5,
128.0, 127.2, 121.7, 121.1, 118.1 (q, J C-F = 318 Hz), 70.1, 58.5, 52.8,
17.3; HRMS (LSI) calcd for C26H24F3N2O7S: 565.1256; found: 565.1256.
Anal. Calcd for C26H23F3N2O7S: C, 55.32; H, 4.11; N, 4.96. Found: C,
55.32, H, 4.17; N, 4.98.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM anaerobic, stereoselective, Stille coupling reaction, 85:15 mixt. of
amide rotamers
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic Asymmetric Synthesis of Quaternary Carbons Bearing Two Aryl
Substituents. Enantioselective Synthesis of 3-Alkyl-3-Aryl Oxindoles by
Catalytic Asymmetric Intramolecular Heck Reactions
