$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 2-Vinyl-1H-indole-3-carboxylate (21); Conventional Stille Coupling
from 18. In a 25 mL, oven-dried, single-neck round bottomed flask
equipped with a magnetic stirring bar and a rubber septum were placed
2-iodoindole 1819 (0.015 g, 0.050 mmol), tributyl(vinyl)tin (0.032 g,
0.100 mmol), tetrakis(triphenylphosphine) palladium (0.004 g, 0.003 mmol)
and CuDPP (0.014 g, 0.050 mmol) inside the glovebox. This flask was
connected to a reflux condenser and flushed with a stream of N2 for 5
minutes. Anhydrous acetonitrile (5.0 mL) was added to above mixture via
syringe and the resultant green solution was heated at 70 °C in an oil
bath for 6 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt and filtered over a
small pad of Celite and the filtrate was concentrated to give a green
residue. Silica gel chromatography (20% ethyl acetate in hexanes)
afforded 21 as clear oil, identified by NMR comparison with the reported
data.21 0.009 g (90%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille reaction, glove box used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stille Coupling of an Aziridinyl Stannatrane
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Theddu, Naresh; Vedejs, Edwin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2013), 78(10), 5061-5066

