$DATUM Dimethyl-2,2:6,2-terpyridines. Route 1: The
methyl-2-tributylstannylpyridine 2a-c (3 g, 7.85 mmol),
2,6-dibromopyridine 1 (0.75 g, 3.17 mmol) and
tetrakis-(triphenylphosphine)-palladium(0) (0.29 g, 6.0 mol%) are
refluxed for 4 days in absolute toluene (50 mL). After removal of the
solvent, the black residue is treated with aq HCl (6 M). The suspension
is extracted with CH2Cl2 and the organic phase is washed again with HCl
(6 M). The aq solution is added dropwise into cold aq ammonia (10%). The
precipitate is filtered off, dissolved in CH2Cl2, dried over Na2SO4, the
solvent is removed again and the residue is crystallized from ethyl
acetate. 4, white crystal, yield 90% (Lit.15 67%). Mp 173 °C (Lit.15
169-171 °C, Lit.15 174-175 °C). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ = 2.39 (s, 6 H, CH3),
7.63 (dd, J = 8.01, 2.28 Hz, 2 H, H4,4''), 7.91 (t, J = 7.82 Hz, 1 H,
H4'), 8.38 (d, J = 7.62 Hz, 2 H, H3',5'), 8.49 (d, J = 8.40 Hz, 2 H,
H3,3''), 8.50 (s, 2 H, H6,6''). C17H15N3 (261.32): Calcd C, 78.13; H,
5.79; N, 16.08. Found: C, 77.92; H, 5.73; N, 16.07.
