$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Small Scale Coupling (Scheme 2 and Table 3);
Preparation of 6 Using Conditions A. In a 25 mL, ovendried, single-neck
round bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic stirring bar and a rubber
septum was placed aziridinyl stannatrane 8 (0.05 g, 0.05 mmol), methyl
4-bromobenzoate (0.007 g, 0.033 mmol), CuDPP (0.014 g, 0.05 mmol) and
Pd(tBu3P)2 (0.001 g, 0.002 mmol) inside the glovebox. This mixture was
flushed with a stream of N2 and dissolved in dry DMF (3 mL). The
resultant solution was stirred at rt while monitoring for completion of
reaction (typically 4 h). The reaction mixture was diluted with ethyl
acetate (20 mL) and water (15 mL). The layers were separated and the
organic layer was washed with water (3 × 10 mL), dried (MgSO4) and
concentrated. Silica gel chromatography (10% ethyl acetate in hexanes)
afforded 0.015 g (85%) of 6 as clear oil, identical to the material
described above. (2R,3R)-2-(Benzyloxymethyl)-3-phenyl-1-tritylaziridine
(10). Conditions A with 8 (0.055 g, 0.054 mmol) and PhI (0.007 g, 0.036
mmol); silica gel chromatography afforded 10.1a 0.015 g (90%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Stille reaction, glove box used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stille Coupling of an Aziridinyl Stannatrane
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Theddu, Naresh; Vedejs, Edwin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2013), 78(10), 5061-5066

