$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure in the preparation of 3g: A mixture of 3-bromothiophene
(0.5mmole), CuO(0.5mmole) and Pd(PPh3)4(0.025mmole) in 4ml dry DMF was
stirred at 130°C under argon for 30min. The FcSnBu3 (0.55mmole) was added
at 100 °C in one portion. Then the mixture was heated and kept at 120-130
°C for an hour. The mixture was worked up in the above manner, and
afforded 3g, yield 95%. 3g, yield 95%. 1H NMR δ 7.67(d, 1H, J=4.15),
7.16(d, 1H, J=4.15), 4.712(m, 2H), 4.43(m, 2H), 4.21(s, 5H), 2.38(s, 3H);
IR: 3093, 1649, 1528, 1459, 1106, 1002; MS m/z 310(M+, 10%), 309(61%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-catalyzed Stille coupling for the preparation of ferrocenyl
thiophene derivatives
