$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM EXAMPLE 18 (4-Nitrobiphenyl) a) To a stainless steel reactor (10 ml) was
added 4-bromonitrobenzene (200 mg, 1 mmol), trimethylphenyltin (194 mg,
0.81 mmol), encapsulated Pd resin as prepared in Example 1 (20 mg, 4
mmol) and tetrabutylammonium acetate (800 mg, ca 2.6 mmol). This was
sealed under an atmosphere of CO2 (ca. 800 psi). The reaction was heated
at 100°C for 6 h with stirring, upon which the reaction was cooled to
room temperature and vented into a beaker containing EtOAc (50 ml). The
product was adsorbed onto silica and was chromatographed (silica gel,
ethyl acetate-hexane 1:49 as eluent) and afforded a mixture of
4-nitrobiphenyl and unreacted starting material (128 mg, 90%
4-nitrobiphenyl by 1H NMR, 60% 4-nitrobiphenyl by calculation).
(4-Nitrobiphenyl), yield 128 mg, 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM high pressure, supercrit., catalyst was encapsulated, Stille reaction,
optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microencapsulated transition metal reagents for reactions in
supercritical fluids
